//  PRIMARY HAND ONLY. Alt-hand casting is deliberately removed for now: every
//  generated staff rolls a random altAbility, and an ability with no npcIntent
//  patch falls back to "harmful", so the alt branch was aiming at the combat
//  target and overwriting the primary branch's aim in the same tick. Aim
//  position is a single shared resource -- whichever branch writes it last
//  wins. Re-add alt only under this same one-cast-per-tick selector.
//
//  Order below is intent priority: heal, then buff, then attack. Only one leaf
//  may own the aim on any given tick.
//
//  castRangeFallback / castRangeMargin: cast range is read off the equipped
//  ability (vanilla staff abilities declare maxCastRange, all of them 25 tiles).
//  The fallback only applies when an ability declares none; the margin covers
//  the gap between the ability's "focus position" and our entity position.
//
//  requireLineOfSight: heal/buff ally scans reject targets we cannot see. Turn
//  off in walled test arenas where allies sit behind pillars.
//
//  debugTargeting: log every ally candidate with its damage team and each
//  filter result, so you can see which filter rejected whom.
{
  "name": "nicemice_npccombat-wandstaff",
  "description": "",
  "scripts": [
    "/scripts/behavior.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/npc.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/math.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/world.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/movement.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/time.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/position.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/entity.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/nicemice_wandstaff.lua"
  ],
  "parameters": {
    "castRangeFallback": 25,
    "castRangeMargin": 5,
    "validHealingTargetRange": 30,
    "validBuffTargetRange": 30,
    "requireLineOfSight": true,
    "debugTargeting": true,
    "wizardryCooldown_primary": 2.5
  },
